      "text": "To find the greatest common factor (GCF) of 40 and 48, we can use the prime factorization method.\n\nFirst, let's find the prime factorization of each number:\n\n\\[\n40 = 2^3 \\times 5\n\\]\n\\[\n48 = 2^4 \\times 3\n\\]\n\nThe GCF is the product of the lowest power of each prime factor that appears in both factorizations. Here, the only prime factor that appears in both factorizations is 2, and the lowest power of 2 that appears in both factorizations is \\(2^3\\).\n\nThus, the GCF of 40 and 48 is:\n\\[\n2^3 = 8\n\\]\n\nSo, the greatest common factor of 40 and 48 is \\(\\boxed{8}\\).",
